        "text": "=Ticker:  {{ $json.Ticker }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "You are a financial data extraction assistant. Your task is to identify the full company name and business sector for stock ticker symbols.  INSTRUCTIONS: 1. You will receive a stock ticker symbol (e.g., \"AAPL\", \"MSFT\") 2. Return the full company name and primary business sector 3. Use standard sector classifications: Technology, Healthcare, Consumer Cyclical, Consumer Defensive, Financial Services, Communication Services, Energy, Industrials, Basic Materials, Real Estate, Utilities 4. Return ONLY valid JSON in this exact format with no additional text:  {\"companyName\": \"Company Name Here\", \"sector\": \"Sector Here\"}  CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS: - No markdown code blocks - No explanations or commentary - No ```json``` wrapper - Just the raw JSON object - If you don't know the ticker, return: {\"companyName\": \"Unknown\", \"sector\": \"Unknown\"}  EXAMPLES: Input: AAPL Output: {\"companyName\": \"Apple Inc.\", \"sector\": \"Technology\"}  Input: JNJ Output: {\"companyName\": \"Johnson & Johnson\", \"sector\": \"Healthcare\"}  Input: WMT Output: {\"companyName\": \"Walmart Inc.\", \"sector\": \"Consumer Defensive\"} ```  ---  ### **User Prompt (Message):** ``` {{$json.Ticker}} That's it! Just send the ticker symbol.  LLM Chain Node Configuration: Node Name: \"Get Stock Info via AI\"  Chain Type: LLM Chain  Model: Claude Sonnet 4 (or GPT-4)  System Message: (paste the system message above)  Prompt: {{$json.Ticker}}  Output Parser: None (we'll parse JSON in next node)  Code Node After AI - Parse Response: javascript const ticker = $json.Ticker; const aiResponse = $('Get Stock Info via AI').first().json.response ||                     $('Get Stock Info via AI').first().json.output ||                    $('Get Stock Info via AI').first().json.text;  let stockInfo;  try {   // Remove any markdown formatting if present   let cleaned = aiResponse.trim();   cleaned = cleaned.replace(/```json\\n?/g, '').replace(/```\\n?/g, '');      // Parse JSON   stockInfo = JSON.parse(cleaned);    } catch (error) {   console.error(`Failed to parse AI response for ${ticker}:`, aiResponse);   stockInfo = {     companyName: 'Error - Could not parse',     sector: 'Unknown'   }; }  console.log(`${ticker}: ${stockInfo.companyName} - ${stockInfo.sector}`);  return [{   json: {     ticker: ticker,     companyName: stockInfo.companyName,     sector: stockInfo.sector   } }]; Comparison: Aspect\tPolygon API ✅\tAI LLM ⚠️ Accuracy\t100% (real data)\t~95% (may hallucinate) Speed\tFast (1 API call)\tSlower (LLM inference) Cost\tFree/cheap\tAI tokens cost Data Quality\tOfficial, up-to-date\tDepends on training data Reliability\tVery reliable\tMay fail to parse JSON Extra Data\tMarket cap, exchange, SIC codes\tJust name & sector My Strong Recommendation: 🎯 Use the Polygon API approach (first workflow)  Why:  Your Polygon subscription already gives you this data More accurate and reliable Faster execution No AI token costs Gets you additional useful data (market cap, exchange, etc.) Quick Implementation: Google Sheets Structure: A (Ticker)\tB (Company Name)\tC (Sector)\tD (Market Cap) AAPL\t← Fill this\t← Fill this\t← Fill this MSFT\t← Fill this\t← Fill this\t← Fill this ...\t\t\t Nodes Needed: Manual Trigger Google Sheets Read (Column A only) HTTP Request (Polygon ticker details) Code (Extract data) Google Sheets Update (Write to columns B, C, D) Which approach do you want to use?  Option A: Polygon API (recommended) ✅ Option B: AI LLM (if you insist) Let me know and I'll give you the exact node-by-node setup! "
            }
          ]
        },
